{"kind":"finding","id":"F-ledger-career-027-01","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/ContractsModuleTests.cs","line":260,"method":"TerminalContractActionTypes_TrackLatestTerminalOutcome","category":"T3","severity":"Medium","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/GameActions/ContractsModule.cs:509; set terminalContractActions[id]/terminalContractOutcomes[id] only when the key is absent (first-wins) -> this cell stays green, since c1/c2/c3/c4 each record exactly one terminal action","what_it_asserts":"The terminal-action and terminal-outcome maps carry Completed/Failed/Cancelled for c1/c2/c3 and DeadlineExpired for c4 (reached through CheckDeadlines).","why_weak":"Every contract id receives exactly one terminal action, so the 'latest outcome wins' behavior the name claims is never discriminated: a first-wins guard on the two maps passes unchanged. Those maps drive KspStatePatcher's tombstone discrimination (ContractsModule.cs:50-59).","proposed_action":"Add a cell that fails then cancels one id with no intervening Accept (a re-accept clears both maps at ContractsModule.cs:378-379) and assert the maps end on ContractCancel/Cancelled.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"coverage","sut":"ContractsModule","sut_file":"Source/Parsek/GameActions/ContractsModule.cs","sut_line":244,"case_kind":"state-transition","proposed_name":"PrePass_DuplicateActiveAccept_TracksTheLatestAccept","sketch":"var module = new ContractsModule(); var a1 = new GameAction { Type = GameActionType.ContractAccept, UT = 100, ContractId = \"c1\", DeadlineUT = 500f, FundsPenalty = 100f }; var a2 = new GameAction { Type = GameActionType.ContractAccept, UT = 200, ContractId = \"c1\", DeadlineUT = 900f, FundsPenalty = 700f }; var actions = new List<GameAction> { a1, a2, new GameAction { Type = GameActionType.FundsEarning, UT = 1000 } }; module.PrePass(actions); var injected = actions[actions.Count - 1]; Assert.Equal(GameActionType.ContractFail, injected.Type); Assert.Equal(900f, (float)injected.UT); Assert.Equal(700f, injected.FundsPenalty);","guards":"The tracked[id] = action overwrite at ContractsModule.cs:244 (and activeContracts[id] = action at :376). Ignoring a duplicate still-active accept instead of overwriting leaves the first accept's deadline and penalties on the books; Accept_Duplicate_LogsWarning (ContractsModuleTests.cs:487) only reads the warn log and no cell re-accepts an active id with different values.","risk":"career"}
